VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'But whatever it is, these Space Marines only use simple faction color cues. Yes , we still get edge highlighting, scuffs, and some battle damage. The emblems of the order are clearly depicted on the knees. The metallic areas'

[11:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hint at NMM, or non-metallic metal, style printing. This is an artistic painting technique. You can search Google for an explanation. This is not the same video. But the input prompts definitely need improvement. And that\'s why'

[11:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hand-painted models will surpass what AI can do. At least for now. And yes, I think an apt description for all of them would be that some colors look pale. It\'s almost as if the models'

[12:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'are covered in too much matte polish. And the surface texture seems to contribute to this too, as the more you move the model in the light, the more light is reflected from different angles. A satin or even glossy varnish can'

[12:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'bring back some of the color. But this softness is usually part of the result. And yes, most of these models came out a little dark. But I attribute this to the fact that the generator creates them expecting them to be used in a'

[12:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'lit game scene, not as a raw output from a printer. So, besides digital painting being a skill, we also need to understand how color reproduction works on these machines so that what we see on screen is closer'

[12:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to what we get when we print. This is still ahead. And even in FDM printing, where a full spectrum of filaments is used to color models by mixing filaments, people quickly learn that filament opacity is'

[12:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'almost as important as the color itself. And if not, I\'ll release a video about it soon. But I have to be honest, guys. I would call them acceptable. They are suitable for a gaming table as a recognizable squad or army. But they definitely don\'t have that'

[13:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'neat, drawn look or clean lines. But yeah, look, I know. Many who watch will exclaim, " This doesn\'t look like a well-painted miniature at all." And yes, I agree. Others will say, "They\'re better than anything'

