AUDIO: 'model them, refine them, and print them. The family gets a really cool souvenir that, at least for now, no one else has. And let\'s be honest, friends, I know a lot of people hate this, but AI will take over three of'

[15:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'these stages of work. And these prints don\'t have to win art contests to make a great gift. They just have to be human-like and bring joy. But speaking of painting, I finally had this head of Gustav, the'

[15:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'character from Expedition 33. By the way, if you haven\'t played it, it\'s the best Final Fantasy game since Part 10. This model was created by Casey Studio, and I have already managed to paint the polymer version of it. So I printed the head in'

[15:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'white to compare the detail, and also with AI colors to compare them to my painting. I think we can look at both options and say that each is better than the other in its own way . Casey Studio'

[16:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'also shared their color version, which I printed on a smaller scale to save time and get this video out faster . It would take forever, even if HeyGears were printed. They have other tasks besides'

[16:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'serving me, but that changes the comparison by scale. But that\'s exactly what I was saying earlier about color. The result was not what we expected, which proves: for high-quality painting, experience with these machines is needed to'

[16:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'properly adjust the colors. So please don\'t scold anyone for this. It was literally an experiment of three people playing " broken phone." He sent it to me, I sent it to HeyGears, and they printed it. By the way, I know that in the'

[16:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'USA this game is called " telephone". We call it the "broken phone," but for the sake of political correctness and my friends in China, I\'ll just say it\'s called "Whisper." But yes, this specimen didn\'t come out with perfect colors , but I must say that this is definitely the'

[16:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'future for those who create such sculptures. So, modelers, if you\'re not already working on converting your library to color, or at least coloring your models , I\'ll get back to why this is important in a moment. I want'

[17:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to discuss what this means for us now in the context of these machines ? Well, look, if you know me, I\'ll be frank with you. I love to paint. That\'s how I got involved in all this. Therefore, quickly getting a finished figure is not my main'

[17:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'goal. But I can\'t look at these models of my family or the comparison to the J55 and not be impressed. And I\'m actually happy with where it\'s going, because FDM still makes sense for larger,'

[17:24] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'more functional parts. For me, polymer printing definitely remains the best for the finest details on models that I want to print and then paint. But I really think this technology deserves its'

[17:36] [scene:talk]
